<section id="pioneer"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="eyebrow">From learning relevance to scalable data-driven AI, 2001–2015</div>
  <h2>Before the term existed</h2>
  <p>The program began before Google with a deeper question than dataset size: can a machine learn what should count as relevant? SVMActive (2001) treated the user's image-query concept as something to be learned from relevance feedback. Dynamic Partial Function (DPF, 2002–2003) challenged the assumption of a single fixed global similarity metric, allowing different image pairs to be judged similar through different subsets of perceptual features. EXTENT (2005) further connected context, visual content, and semantic ontology in a learned multimodal semantic model.</p>
  <p>At Google Research, this data-driven view became a web-scale engineering program: large-scale image annotation, distributed learning infrastructure, and a family of parallel machine-learning algorithms. The 2010 DMD paper made the thesis explicit by combining a deep model-based pipeline with a data-driven pipeline, and the 2011 Springer book <a href="https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-642-20429-6"><i>Foundations of Large-Scale Multimedia Information Management and Retrieval</i></a> consolidated the conceptual, data, and scalable-learning strands. The line later extended to efficient edge inference in 2014 and parallel deep convolutional neural networks in 2015.</p>
  <div class="timeline">
    <div class="card"><div class="yr">2001</div><h3>SVMActive</h3><p>Learned a user's latent image-query concept from actively selected relevance feedback.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="yr">2002–03</div><h3>Dynamic Partial Function</h3><p>Learned transformation-tolerant, pair-dependent perceptual similarity rather than imposing one fixed global metric.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="yr">2005</div><h3>EXTENT</h3><p>Fused context, visual content, and semantic ontology in a learned multimodal semantic model.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="yr">2007</div><h3>Parallel SVM</h3><p>Scaled support-vector-machine learning across distributed systems.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="yr">2008</div><h3>Large-scale image annotation</h3><p>30K+ web images learned from visual, textual, query, and usage-associated signals using distributed LDA and MapReduce.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="yr">2008</div><h3>Parallel LDA</h3><p>Distributed Gibbs sampling and topic learning on MapReduce.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="yr">2008–10</div><h3>Parallel spectral clustering</h3><p>Large-scale graph partitioning on distributed infrastructure.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="yr">2009–10</div><h3>Parallel frequent-pattern mining</h3><p>Scalable frequent-pattern mining; the PFP lineage later entered Apache Spark.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="yr">2009–11</div><h3>ImageNet support</h3><p>Google Research support for Fei-Fei Li's ImageNet project, a distinct public dataset and benchmark contribution.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="yr">2010</div><h3>DMD</h3><p>Explicit deep model-based plus data-driven hybrid architecture for image annotation.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="yr">2011</div><h3>Springer synthesis</h3><p>Consolidated the data-driven thesis, large-scale multimedia learning, and parallel ML algorithms.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="yr">2014</div><h3>Big Data, Small Footprint</h3><p>Hardware-software co-design for low-power transportation-mode classification on wearables and mobile devices.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="yr">2015</div><h3>SpeeDO</h3><p>Parallelized stochastic gradient descent for deep convolutional neural networks on CPU and GPU clusters.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>
